{"attachments":[{"content_type":"image/png","filename":"unknown.png","id":"865689399696818196","local_path":"discord/empire-city/attachments/859862265125666866/865689399696818196-unknown.png","message_id":"865689400020172830","sha256":"55c3a9b22dd03fdefe974dd98b07a8e7f8d897ada6304e2cefbd7dc1f7840940","size":786549,"url":"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/859862265125666866/865689399696818196/unknown.png?ex=6ac0bad4&is=6abf6954&hm=646444926ca6452bb785efe041f4f73e21f05fa32c8a22ce42aa9e16f9a99bcd&"}],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"859862265125666866","content":"Once each player has made a skill check, and you know if they are caught unaware, Chimeric Sewer Rats pour out of holes (share the above photo), there are 2 rats per player, and will fight 2 to a player.  If the players failed the skill challenge, the rats initiative is 20.  Otherwise it is 1.  Have the players roll initiative.  The rats pair up one each player.  One rat of each pair will use the help action, the other will attack, as long as there are two rats on the player.  The rats are aware of the players and are not surprised.  These rats have a fly speed equal to half their walk speed.\n\nAnytime a rat dies, its body liquifies into a pool of organic goo.  Once observed, the player with the highest Arcana may roll Arcana to identify what they are seeing.  The DC is 15, and if successful, they will know the goo is tied to Aberrations and Oozes.  That is all the info that can be gleaned atthis time.\n\nAt the beginning of the rats initiative count, every 2 piles of goo will recombine at a player (generally the person nearest the two piles, or pick a player) and will always attempt to recombine next to another rat so it can use pack tactics ability.  These new rats have 2 heads, 2 tails, 8 rat legs, 8 spider legs, 4 wings and use the “Diseased Giant Rat” stat block (can no longer fly).\n\nThen when these Diseased Giant Rats die, again they turn to a pile of goo.  At this point, allow the player with the highest Medicine to make a check.  If they hit 12 or higher, let them know that this goo appears more unstable than the previous goo.\n\nWhen there are two Diseased Giant Rat goo piles, at the top of the rats initiative, they once again recombine.  But this time they will try to recombine on a player that has not been diseased by a diseased rat (double preference if there is another rat on said person).  Use the “Diseased Rat Swarm” stat block, but describe it as the following: 4 heads, 4 tails, 16 rat legs, 16 spider legs, 8 wings and as large as a dog, and definitely can not fly anymore.  When it dies, its body does not liquify, but stays as the corpse of this abomination.  **If there is an odd number of players, there will be one giant rat that doesn’t get to combine.  This is as intended.  No matter the number of players, this encounter is considered a medium difficulty and is supposed to force players to use some resources, hurt people, and make them have to deal with the ongoing disease that the rats can pass on.**  Make sure that if players get low on hp, you should spread the attacks.  They can smell the disease on people, and want to spread it.  Anyone that is bitten by any of these rats will gain one level of Hampstead Damnation at the end of the event (for ease of running), but will not gain more damnation from these rats.","created_at":"2021-07-16T20:20:36.696000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"865689400020172830","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
